From: Pietro Ameruoso <p.ameruoso@live.it>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 08:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: as21xxx: discard stale C45 read response

The first C45 response returned by the AS21xxx belongs to the preceding
MDIO transaction. The existing workaround performs the required write
after the read, but still returns that stale first response to callers.
This makes runtime status reads unreliable even though PHY matching can
succeed with repeated reads.

Discard the first response, perform the workaround write, and issue the
C45 read again. Keep a second workaround write after the returned read so
the following transaction starts from the same known state.

Signed-off-by: Pietro Ameruoso <p.ameruoso@live.it>
---
 drivers/net/phy/as21xxx.c | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/phy/as21xxx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/as21xxx.c
@@ -973,10 +973,13 @@ static int as21xxx_read_mmd(struct phy_d
 	struct mii_bus *bus = phydev->mdio.bus;
 	int val;
 
-	val = __mdiobus_c45_read(bus, phydev->mdio.addr, devad,
-				 regnum);
+	/* The first C45 response belongs to the preceding transaction. */
+	__mdiobus_c45_read(bus, phydev->mdio.addr, devad, regnum);
+
+	__mdiobus_write(bus, 0x0, MII_BMSR, 0x1);
+
+	val = __mdiobus_c45_read(bus, phydev->mdio.addr, devad, regnum);
 
-	/* FIXME: verify if it's actually ok to limit this to MII_BMSR */
 	__mdiobus_write(bus, 0x0, MII_BMSR, 0x1);
 
 	return val;
